    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who anchors the lineup with an elite 73.66 efficiency score. Facing Grant Holmes (4.71 xERA) in a favorable park environment, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a massive +14% platoon boost and a +8% order premium, making him our highest-upside play for both power and efficiency. Following him, **Jacob Wilson** (59.39) and **Kyle Tucker** (59.83) provide strong, high-floor profiles. While **Kyle Tucker** faces a disciplined arm in Bryan Woo, the wind blowing out at the venue provides a crucial lift, helping him maintain high utility despite a tougher matchup. Similarly, **Drake Baldwin** is a priority start; his leadoff positioning against Jake Irvin (3.99 xERA) gives him an excellent runway to accumulate Runs, provided he secures that #1 spot in the confirmed lineup.\n\nStrategic decisions for this lineup involved balancing our heavy emphasis on SB efficiency against the volatility of today\u2019s matchups. **Nasim Nunez** (56.96) remains a viable inclusion despite the #9 spot because his matchup against Grant Holmes offers the highest SP skill advantage (+17%) of the day, maximizing his potential to swipe bags against a favorable battery. The most difficult bench decision involved choosing between the lower-scoring **Liam Hicks** (41.72) and our other utility options; **Liam Hicks** remains in the C1 slot due to position scarcity, though his start is tempered by a 35% rain risk. We continue to monitor the weather closely for **Jorge Polanco**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Liam Hicks**, as any washout in those contests would necessitate immediate pivots to preserve our dwindling game caps.",
